<title>CANADA: Westcoast, Pacific discuss deal.</title>
<headline>Westcoast, Pacific discuss deal.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pacific Northern Gas Ltd is in discussions to acquire natural gas distribution operations in Fort St. John, British Columbia and certain tax losses from Westcoast Energy Inc, the two companies said on Monday.</p>
<p>Westcoast is Pacific's controlling shareholder. The gas operation services about 8,000 residential and commercial customers with a rate base of about C$15 million.</p>
<p>Prospective terms of the deal and amount of the tax losses were not released. The transfer of ownership would allow cost savings to customers, the companies said.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314</p>
</text>
